+<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
+<title>Check a new assessment · Practice data</title><style>body{max-width:48rem;margin:4vh auto;padding:1rem;color:#20343a;font:1.05rem/1.55 system-ui}h1{font-size:2rem;line-height:1.16}a{color:#135c72}li{margin:.7rem 0}aside{border-left:4px solid #ce4549;padding:.1rem 1rem;background:#fbf5f4}small{color:#44565c}</style>
+<main><a href="../">Open the assessment dashboard</a><h1>Check a new assessment with practice files</h1><aside>These small, invented features test the calculations. Use a separate practice event. They do not describe a real flood, clinic, building or road.</aside>
+<h2>Download the inputs</h2><ul><li><a download href="practice-boundary.geojson">Assessment boundary</a></li><li><a download href="practice-flood.geojson">Dated flood outline</a></li><li><a download href="practice-osm.geojson">OSM-format practice extract</a></li></ul>
+<h2>Run the check</h2><ol><li>Open <strong>New event</strong>. Enter <strong>Practice flood</strong>, country <strong>Mozambique</strong>, hazard <strong>Flood</strong>, and trigger <strong>2 January 2026 at 06:00 UTC</strong>. Create the preliminary brief. The cutoff should be 3 January at 06:00 UTC; numerical exposure is still unknown.</li>
+<li>Open <strong>Assess</strong>. Keep <strong>First 24 hours</strong>. Import the boundary and flood outline under their matching labels. Use the primary button to save the map result without fetching OSM. Expect about <strong>4.65 km²</strong> of mapped flooding. Road and service exposure should still be unknown.</li>
+<li>Open <strong>Assess</strong> again and import the OSM-format file. Its training snapshot is 1 January 2026 at 00:00 UTC. Confirm that this fixture covers the practice area and calculate. Expect <strong>one mapped clinic, one building and about 1.05 km of road</strong> inside the flood area. The mapped school is outside the flood area. Population remains unknown. No external data request is required.</li>
+<li>Use <strong>Print brief</strong> or download the figures. To continue in a new tab later, choose <strong>Sources &amp; data → Export current event</strong> and re-open that file with <strong>Import data</strong>.</li></ol>
+<small>If the file dates are not present in the form, use the fixture metadata: flood observation 2 January 2026 08:00 UTC; release 09:00 UTC the same day. Use UTC or convert to the local time zone shown by the map-date controls.</small></main>
